# SYNTHETIC fixture. Not a captured sweep.
# Hand-built because the prober never writes this shape: it skips a sample
# that bound no values on purpose, so that a sampleSize of 0 cannot be
# misread as "this endpoint has no classes". A store assembled from another
# source, or a later prober that changes its mind, can still hold one, and
# the read query has to answer it honestly either way.
# Exists to make the OPTIONAL around sw:sampledValue in
# web/queries/endpoint_content.rq testable: make sw:sampledValue required
# and this sample vanishes from the answer entirely, so the caller sees
# sampled = False and cannot tell "sampled, found nothing" apart from "no
# run ever sampled this endpoint", which is the whole distinction the
# sampled flag exists to carry. Every other test in this suite stays green
# under that mutation.
